 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 526566,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Your bedroom floor has an area of 25 m<sup>2</sup>. The living room floor measures 600 cm by 750 cm. How many square meters of carpet do you need to buy to carpet the floors in both rooms?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Step 1: Convert the dimensions of the living room to meters.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"600\\cancel{{{\\rm{centimeters}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{{\\rm{1\\ meter}}}}{{100{\\rm{ }}\\cancel{{{\\rm{centimeters}}}}}}} \\right) = 6{\\rm{\\ meters}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"750\\cancel{{{\\rm{centimeters}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{{\\rm{1\\ meter}}}}{{100{\\rm{ }}\\cancel{{{\\rm{centimeters}}}}}}} \\right) = 7.5{\\rm{\\ meters}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2. Find the area of the living room.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A{\\rm{ }} = {\\rm{ }}L{\\rm{ }} \\times {\\rm{ }}W{\\rm{ }} = {\\rm{ }}\\left( {{\\rm{6\\ m}}} \\right)\\left( {7.5{\\rm{\\ m}}} \\right){\\rm{ }} = 45{\\rm{\\ }}{{\\rm{m}}^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 3: Add the result to the provided area of the bedroom.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"25{\\rm{\\ }}{{\\rm{m}}^2} + 45{\\rm{\\ }}{{\\rm{m}}^2} = 70{\\rm{\\ }}{{\\rm{m}}^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>You need to buy 70 square meters of carpet.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "70 m<sup>2</sup>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
